{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"agent_message","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\n**R2-N6 is fixed. R2-N5 is partially fixed.** Four blockers remain:\n\n- **N7 — high:** [validate_scope.go:144](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3932406016/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go:144). Dependency and descendant widening runs only for unmapped changes. Deleting `p/a` beneath surviving module `p` selects `p`, but can carry a consumer declaring `dependsOn: [\"p/a\"]`. Similarly, a changed gitlink matching a discovered parent module can leave its nested modules carried.\n- **N8 — high:** [validate_scope.go:207](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3932406016/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go:207). A declared dependency `\".\"` never matches ordinary root files. After deleting the root manifest, a self-contained consumer depending on `\".\"` can carry results despite changed root inputs.\n- **N9 — high:** [validate_scope.go:135](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3932406016/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go:135). Selection uses lexical paths, while `moduleOverrides` accepts symlink directories through `os.Stat`. An override aliasing module `a` can retain its old result when `a` changes. Account for resolved aliases or conservatively refuse their reuse.\n- **N10 — high:** [validate.go:1423](/var/tmp/pose-work-go/pose-review-run-3932406016/worktree/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go:1423). `material_clean` does not verify that HEAD stayed at the recorded commit. A concurrent committed fix can make checks pass while the record names the earlier failing head. Reverting that fix later can let carry reuse the false pass. Bind cleanliness and provenance to the captured head.\n\nThese findings follow from code inspection; writable scratch was unavailable for additional reproduction fixtures.\n\nFocused and broader tests, race tests, vet, and strict artifact-check passed. Both required matrix runs failed on sandbox write restrictions. The sealed canonical result records 236 passes; fresh required-tool validation remains unmet.\n\nApplied the review workflow, backend-go, security, documentation-style and delivery-evidence rules. No repository changes or attestation were made.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"changes-requested\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N7\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\n      \"line\": 144,\n      \"summary\": \"A discovered owner bypasses dependency and descendant path widening. Deleting nested module p/a beneath surviving module p selects only p; a selfContained consumer depending on p/a stays carried because underDeclaredDependency is called only in the unmapped branch. A changed gitlink matching a discovered parent similarly fails to select nested modules beneath it. Apply dependency and ancestor intersections independently of single-owner matching and add both regressions.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N8\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\n      \"line\": 207,\n      \"summary\": \"underDeclaredDependency does not treat '.' as the project root: ordinary root filenames match neither '.' nor './...'. After removing the root manifest, a selfContained consumer with dependsOn:['.'] can remain carried despite changed or deleted root inputs. Handle root dependency ownership explicitly and test removal of the root manifest.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N9\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\n      \"line\": 135,\n      \"summary\": \"Lexical ownership does not account for filesystem aliases. validate.go:1102 accepts a symlink directory as a moduleOverrides module, but changes under its resolved target select only the target's lexical owner. An alias-specific check can therefore retain an old pass after its actual inputs change. Resolve module aliases for invalidation or conservatively refuse carry for them; cover symlink aliases and case aliases where the filesystem supports them.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"N10\",\n      \"severity\": \"high\",\n      \"disposition\": \"blocker\",\n      \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate.go\",\n      \"line\": 1423,\n      \"summary\": \"material_clean combines cleanliness checks against potentially different HEADs without comparing the final head to run.GitHead. If validation captures failing head H0, a concurrent actor commits a fix H1 before the affected check executes, and the run finishes clean at H1, the pass is recorded as a clean observation of H0. A later revert to H0's source can produce an empty material diff and carry that false pass. Invalidate carry eligibility and material bindings when the captured head changes during the run.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R2-N5\",\n      \"status\": \"partial\",\n      \"evidence\": \"TestCarryDeletedDependencySelectsItsDependents passed and validate_scope.go:158 covers unowned deleted dependency paths. The check is bypassed when a surviving containing module owns those paths, and underDeclaredDependency does not match root dependency '.'. N7 and N8 document the remaining cases.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"R2-N6\",\n      \"status\": \"fixed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate_scope.go:49-53 returns unreadable/undecodable metadata errors; computeChangedScope propagates them and planCarry falls back. TestCarryRejectsUndecodableMetadata passed, including its changed-from exit-2 assertion.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Reviewed the complete subject against R1-R10 and D1-D3, including prior regressions, gitlink ancestor changes, submodule status handling, symlink and conditional case aliases, case-only Git rename handling, manifestless moduleOverrides, nested modules and removed dependencies, stack/check identity changes with an unchanged matrix digest, criticality widening, chained origin preservation, base eligibility, administrative exclusions, dispatch/cancellation, canonical publication guards and atomic replacement, delivery freshness, legacy parsing, manuals and scaffold copies. Existing focused and broader validation-related tests, focused race tests and vet passed. New scenarios were established by code inspection; readonly scratch prevented additional fixtures, including a case-insensitive filesystem or two-writer runtime probe. No separate defect was established in atomic canonical publication itself. Repository remained unchanged.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assumption-integrity\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N10\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Verified dirty-base and dirty-engine guards and documented declaration assumptions. Clean endpoints do not establish that the run observed its recorded head when HEAD moves during validation. N7-N9 additionally invalidate the unchanged-input premise.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-concurrency\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N10\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Worker dispatch and atomic canonical publication were inspected and focused race tests passed, but concurrent committed source changes can produce a false material_clean claim.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-contracts\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected additive JSON fields, canonical-output restrictions, legacy parsing and per-check delivery origins. Existing records retain their interpretation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-input-errors\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Verified incompatible-flag refusals, revision confinement, malformed-base fallback and propagation of metadata decoding failures. Focused negative fixtures passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N7\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Nested provider changes and gitlink ancestor changes can bypass consumer invalidation before delivery results receive current material provenance.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"backend-observability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected metadata error context, fallback reasons, selected-module explanations, carried counts and original observation fields. Existing diagnostic fixtures passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"compatibility\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reviewed additive CLI/file fields, explicit flag restrictions, old-base rejection and legacy delivery fallback. No MCP signature changed; undecodable metadata rejection is explicitly specified.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"correctness\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N7\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Existing fixtures pass, but discovered-owner matching can suppress required dependency and descendant invalidation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"design-causality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N7\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Module-level reuse addresses repeated full execution, but D1 requires complete invalidation of carried inputs. Restricting dependency intersections to unowned changes breaks that causal guarantee.\",\n      \"mappings\": [\n        {\n          \"delta\": \"SD-a9e60b2a\",\n          \"basis\": \"D1\",\n          \"disposition\": \"mapped\",\n          \"rationale\": \"The ADR records original-observation reuse and its unchanged-input premise; D2 and D3 provide engine/matrix comparison and self-containment policy.\"\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"documentation\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared English and Portuguese manuals, help, embedded copies, spec and ADR. They consistently state the intended contracts and fallback behavior. The English embedded-copy difference is the instance-specific Contributor Mode section.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operability\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Inspected actionable canonical-path refusals, metadata decoding errors, full-run fallback explanations and explain output. Existing diagnostic tests passed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"requirements\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N7\",\n      \"rationale\": \"R6 requires declared dependency ownership and changed-path ancestor invalidation without the current unmapped-only restriction. N8 also violates root dependency ownership, and N10 undermines R2.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scope\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-19561aa1521df8c9\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Compared implementation, tests, governance and documentation changes with the spec's affected areas and artifact declarations. Changes remain within the approved carry feature.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"security\",\n      \"disposition\": \"finding\",\n      \"evidence\": \"N10\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Revision and output-path confinement remain intact, but an observation of different committed material can be marked clean for the recorded head and later acquire current evidence authority.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"solution-proportionality\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"structure:design-19561aa1521df8c9\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Reusing module selection and whole-matrix comparison is smaller than per-check manifests or output caching, and chained carries retain bounded original-origin fields. The approach remains sufficient only with complete dependency/alias invalidation and a trustworthy captured-head binding; the blockers identify those missing conditions.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"artifact-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-carries-unchanged-checks --strict\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Exited 0 with 15 claims, 20 observations and 985 reported findings. Its trailer head d286747c differs from the sealed checkout only in delivery-integrity.json, generation.json and spec-graph.json.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-design\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Used supplied sealed structural evidence and inspected the ADR and complete diff. Writable scratch for isolated assessment execution was unavailable.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-discover\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Assessment publication would change files. Scratch creation failed with a read-only filesystem error.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-integrate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Writable scratch was unavailable for this publishing assessment. Inspected result production, delivery parsing and material-freshness consumers directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\",\n      \"disposition\": \"not-used\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Writable scratch was unavailable for this publishing assessment; no assessment output was written into the sealed checkout.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"closeout-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion-only tool requires the recorded review conclusion. No attestation was recorded.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-check\",\n      \"disposition\": \"deferred\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Completion-only tool requires the recorded review conclusion. No attestation was recorded.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suggest-review\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"passed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\",\n      \"rationale\": \"Resolved and consulted backend-go, security and documentation-style rules; additionally applied delivery-evidence and consumed relevant knowledge.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"This ref identifies the supplied sealed canonical pass, not a fresh local pass. Ran pose validate --strict; it exited 1 with 236 failures because child checks could not create build directories or write caches. The committed canonical record reports 236 passes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"validate\",\n      \"component\": \"pose-mcp\",\n      \"disposition\": \"failed\",\n      \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\n      \"rationale\": \"This ref identifies the supplied sealed canonical pass, not a fresh local pass. Ran pose validate --strict --module pose-mcp; it exited 1 with 233 failures caused by sandbox write restrictions. Independent focused and broader tests, focused race tests and vet passed.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}}
